; ============================================================
; Simple-Calc  —  STELLAR calculator app  (loads at $4000, VM1)
; VERSION:  v04   (Step 3b, minimal: just Ans retention)
; ============================================================
; Scope reduction:
;   v04 pass-1 & pass-2 (chained ops + Ans + overflow bundled)
;   both failed at 2+2 with the VM ending past HALT.  Suspicion:
;   the newly-introduced $DA op-dispatcher with CALL from parser
;   + IFTRUEL to op handlers + RETURN from handler didn't play
;   well with STELLAR's CALL/RETURN mechanics.  Chained ops
;   needed too much new plumbing at once to bisect.
;
;   This build is a MINIMAL v04: just v03 pass-5 with Ans
;   retention added.  Chained ops and overflow deferred to v05.
;
; ---- ANS RETENTION ----
;   In the line-complete dispatch, if the first char is
;   + - * or /, branch to LBL $56 (Ans entry).  $56 loads R7
;   from $4830 (stored Ans), reads the first char into R8 (the
;   pending op), advances R3, sets R9=0, then GTL $54 (state B —
;   parse the RHS number).  From there the existing v03 flow
;   handles it: state B parses the number, $55 dispatches on R8,
;   op handler computes, result tail prints.
;
;   +10 bytes to dispatch (4 new TESTAI+IFTRUEL pairs)
;   +40 bytes for LBL $56 body
;   Total v04 = 854 bytes; HALT at $4355.
;
; ---- vCPU REGISTERS (same as v03) ----
;   R1 write ptr    R2 base ($4800)    R3 result/scan
;   R4 scratch     R5 '0'    R6 '9'
;   R7 first num / Ans in Ans mode / decimal-print flag in $80
;   R8 op char (low byte)    R9 second num
;   RA string ptr    RB scratch mem ptr
;   RC=10000 RD=1000 RE=100 RF=10
;
; ---- MEMORY MAP ----
;   $4000..$4355  code (HALT at $4355)
;   $4195-$4196   self-mod SUBAI in $99 (negate for signed print)
;   $4295-$4296   self-mod SUBAI in $61 ('-' operator)
;   $4700..$472E  strings
;   $4800..       input line buffer
;   $4830..$4831  stored Ans
; ============================================================

; ---- CODE ($4000..$4355, 854 bytes) ----
